Original commit body from 08fafc31dcff9c0da7c0a9d69865eaa62d522fd0:

The enclosing-callable family (WI-kosar): four analyzers found a call's
CALLER by name through the repo-wide NameResolver, whose registry keeps one
symbol per name, so two files defining the same function had one file's
calls credited to the other's.

- zig (INV-musij): the enclosing function is the ``function_declaration``
  that contains the call, by position (``symbol_declared_by``), instead of
  ``resolver.lookup(qualified_name)``.
- llvm_ir (INV-nafij): the caller is the ``define`` at the recorded
  position; the callee is this file's ``define`` first, the registry
  otherwise (a local ``declare`` does not pre-empt another file's define).
  The never-read ``_pending_calls`` store and the symbols/calls dual-purpose
  walk are gone: Pass 1 extracts symbols, Pass 2 collects calls.
- cobol (INV-lutaj): the caller is the paragraph OR section whose header
  last preceded the statement, by position (a section header used not to
  update it); a PERFORM/CALL target binds inside the performing program
  first, then this file, then the registry.
- tlaplus (INV-razus residual): a referenced name binds a LET-local, then
  THIS spec's definition, then the registry; ``Bar == Init`` in spec B no
  longer points at spec A's ``Init``.
- agda: a referenced name binds this file's definition before the
  registry's (``B.zero -> A.Nat`` on two files each defining ``Nat``).

Each analyzer gains a two-file same-name fixture. The item's proposed
regex gate on ``resolver.lookup(<caller-ish name>)`` was tried and not
added: 11 of its 13 hits on the tree are legitimate callee lookups, so it
would be a baseline of waivers rather than a gate.

Test fixture note: tree-sitter-agda loses the declaration that follows a
``data ... where`` block in the fixture's layout, so the Agda fixture uses
``postulate``; the loss itself is filed separately.

